                                        "entry_id": "65d1bd07-ebbe-3a29-8b5b-8b0e3e337ce0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outwork. A fortification outside a castle used to split an attacking force; composed of two faces, forming a salient angle whose gorge resembles a half-moon"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbf77116-3f17-4ab0-b1b2-98c58a275559",
                                                "sense_id": "8b80bb55-ce3f-3fae-966b-d8ec8d3973ab",
                                                "text": "It is about 2,500 yards in circuit, is built of red stone, and, according to Von Orlich, is now \" a bastioned quinquangle ; the ancient walls with semicircular bastions face the two streams ; the land side is quite regular, and consists of two bastions, and a half-bastion with three ravelins,\" and stands higher than any ground in face of it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
